From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Subject: Revert "Fixes #973: remove DSA/DSS support"

Restore legacy SSH support removed upstream, for talking to old
devices that cannot be upgraded. Shipped only in the separate
paramiko_legacy module; python3-paramiko is untouched.

Forward-ported by hand onto 5.0.0: DSSKey exposes a `private_key`
property instead of its own write_private_key* methods, so it uses
the 5.0 PKey writers (and their new file_format= argument) like
every other key class. Hunks for the since-deleted demos/ dropped.
The upstream changelog hunk is dropped; 5.0.0's changelog is kept.

Origin: vendor, reverts https://github.com/paramiko/paramiko/commit/e534b1abcfe5dd286988d0b347b84a0b902f7461
Forwarded: not-needed
---
